# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

Manages an AI Gateway (AIG) appliance in a Netskope tenant. AIG appliances proxy AI provider and MCP server traffic through Netskope for inspection, policy enforcement, and observability.

After creation the appliance is in `not-registered` status. Use [`netskope_aig_appliance_enrollment_token`](aig_appliance_enrollment_token) to generate a token for registering the appliance.

## Appliance lifecycle

1. Create this resource — note the `id` output.
2. Create a [`netskope_aig_appliance_enrollment_token`](aig_appliance_enrollment_token) using the appliance ID.
3. Install the AIG appliance software on the host and enroll it with the token.
4. After registration, the `status` attribute reflects the connection state.

## Associating AI providers and MCP servers

Add provider or server UUIDs to `ai_provider_ids` and `mcp_server_ids`. Use the [`netskope_aig_ai_provider_list`](../data-sources/aig_ai_provider_list) and [`netskope_aig_mcp_server_list`](../data-sources/aig_mcp_server_list) data sources to look up IDs by name.

